%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3bb5583713e7feb4f8c632285c080082, type: 3}
  m_Name: TodoBoard
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Todo.TodoBoardSO
  Tasks:
  - Category: Architecture
    Name: Define relic runtime architecture and responsibilities
    Description: Decide which classes own relic data runtime state trigger dispatch and player integration so behavior is predictable and extensible.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Architecture
    Name: Define player stat model with base plus modifiers
    Description: Create a stat pipeline that combines base stats and additive or multiplicative modifiers from relics without order bugs.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Data
    Name: Expand RelicSO with id rarity max level and tags
    Description: Add stable identifiers and metadata fields to each relic asset so systems can filter and reference relics safely.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Data
    Name: Add per level effect values and upgrade weighting data
    Description: Store level scaling values and offer weights so each upgrade step can be balanced directly in assets.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Data
    Name: Create RelicCatalogueSO listing all relic definitions
    Description: Build a central catalogue asset used by upgrade generation and content management to avoid scattered references.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Runtime
    Name: Implement RelicInstance runtime state object
    Description: Represent per run relic state like current level cooldown timers stacks and temporary effect state.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Runtime
    Name: Replace placeholder IRelic with lifecycle behavior interface
    Description: Define explicit callbacks for acquire remove level up tick and event driven triggers so all relics share one contract.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Runtime
    Name: Implement RelicInventory as central relic system manager
    Description: Manage owned relic instances add and upgrade flow behavior updates and safe cleanup from one runtime owner.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Runtime
    Name: Add event hub for combat and level related relic triggers
    Description: Publish gameplay events such as enemy killed player hit projectile impact and level up for relics to subscribe to.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Leveling
    Name: Implement player XP and level progression service
    Description: Track xp gains compute next level thresholds and emit level up events with deterministic progression rules.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Leveling
    Name: Trigger upgrade flow when player levels up
    Description: Connect level up events to pause gameplay and open the relic selection flow each time a level threshold is reached.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Upgrades
    Name: Build weighted upgrade offer generator
    Description: Generate a set of upgrade options using rarity and context weights so the choices feel varied but controlled.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Upgrades
    Name: Exclude maxed relics and support upgrade fallback rules
    Description: Prevent invalid offers and provide fallback logic when pools are exhausted to always return valid choices.
    Status: 0
  - Category: UI
    Name: Implement relic selection cards with icon name and description
    Description: Build card visuals and bindings to present each offered relic clearly with readable metadata.
    Status: 0
  - Category: UI
    Name: Wire RelicUpgradeUI choice to relic system apply methods
    Description: Send selected card actions into add or upgrade APIs and close the upgrade flow reliably after selection.
    Status: 0
  - Category: StateMachine
    Name: Implement UpgradeScreenState enter update and exit flow
    Description: Finish state behavior so entering upgrade state shows UI waits for selection and exits back to gameplay correctly.
    Status: 0
  - Category: StateMachine
    Name: Pause and resume gameplay simulation around upgrades
    Description: Freeze active gameplay systems during upgrade decisions and restore simulation once the player confirms a choice.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Combat
    Name: Implement passive stat relic category
    Description: Support relics that immediately modify player or weapon stats and persist those modifiers across levels.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Combat
    Name: Implement triggered relic category on events
    Description: Support relic effects that proc from combat events with cooldown and chance handling.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Combat
    Name: Implement projectile spawning relic category
    Description: Add relics that create and control projectiles including fire rate lifetime damage and targeting behavior.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Combat
    Name: Implement chain effect relic category explosion to lightning
    Description: Implement multi stage effects where one trigger causes secondary and tertiary effects such as explosion then storm ticks.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Performance
    Name: Add pooling for relic spawned projectiles and area effects
    Description: Reuse projectile and area effect objects to reduce allocations and frame spikes during heavy combat.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Content
    Name: Create first five relic assets for vertical slice
    Description: Author a representative starter set of relics covering passive triggered projectile and chain archetypes.
    Status: 0
  - Category: Balancing
    Name: Tune level curve and relic rarity weights
    Description: Adjust progression speed and offer probabilities to keep power growth satisfying without runaway scaling.
    Status: 0
  - Category: QA
    Name: Add playmode tests for add upgrade and max level behavior
    Description: Cover inventory and upgrade lifecycle cases so adding leveling and cap behavior remain stable over changes.
    Status: 0
  - Category: QA
    Name: Validate chain relic interactions and event ordering
    Description: Verify chained effects execute in deterministic order and do not double trigger or miss events.
    Status: 0
